# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# App variables
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Variables of this application only, appended to infra/compose/.env.example
# after the platform's by `platform-infra sync` (this file is APP-OWNED: it is
# created once and never overwritten; .env.example itself is generated). Add a
# variable here as KEY=value with its explanation on the lines above it, then
# run the sync. Never add a commented-out KEY=value line: the deploy wizard
# reads every such line as a declared variable.

# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Identity (deployment values, set by the deploy wizard)
# -----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# No variable is added here: the platform's own template above already declares
# every identity variable, and a second declaration would show twice in the
# deploy wizard. What this deployment sets for them (docs/specs/cloud-app.md,
# section 3.4):
#
# - TENANCY_MODE is single, the template default: one organization, every
#   person joins it as a viewer.
# - INITIAL_ADMIN_EMAIL is the lab owner's own Google address (the placeholder
#   ADMIN_EMAIL in the docs). It skips the allowlist and becomes system admin
#   plus organization admin. Never commit the real address.
# - GOOGLE_CALLBACK_URL is the cloud's public address followed by
#   /api/auth/google/callback, and the Google OAuth client lists exactly that
#   one redirect URI.
# - GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID and GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET come from the Google Cloud
#   console and are never committed.
# - Everyone else is added by address, one at a time, at
#   /admin/settings/allowlist (docs/runbooks/10-lab-operations.md). Never a
#   whole domain.
